DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  mmkksstteemmpp() function generates a unique temporary filename from _t_e_m_‐
       _p_l_a_t_e, creates and opens the file, and returns an open file  descriptor
       for the file.

       The  last six characters of _t_e_m_p_l_a_t_e must be "XXXXXX" and these are re‐
       placed with a string that makes the filename unique.  Since it will  be
       modified,  _t_e_m_p_l_a_t_e  must  not  be a string constant, but should be de‐
       clared as a character array.

       The file is created with permissions 0600, that is, read plus write for
       owner only.  The returned file descriptor provides both read and  write
       access  to  the file.  The file is opened with the ooppeenn(2) OO__EEXXCCLL flag,
       guaranteeing that the caller is the process that creates the file.

       The mmkkoosstteemmpp() function is like mmkksstteemmpp(), with the difference that the
       following bits—with the same meaning as for ooppeenn(2)—may be specified in
       _f_l_a_g_s: OO__AAPPPPEENNDD, OO__CCLLOOEEXXEECC, and OO__SSYYNNCC.  Note that  when  creating  the
       file, mmkkoosstteemmpp() includes the values OO__RRDDWWRR, OO__CCRREEAATT, and OO__EEXXCCLL in the
       _f_l_a_g_s  argument  given  to ooppeenn(2); including these values in the _f_l_a_g_s
       argument given to mmkkoosstteemmpp() is unnecessary,  and  produces  errors  on
       some systems.

       The  mmkksstteemmppss()  function  is like mmkksstteemmpp(), except that the string in
       _t_e_m_p_l_a_t_e contains a suffix of _s_u_f_f_i_x_l_e_n characters.  Thus, _t_e_m_p_l_a_t_e  is
       of  the  form  _p_r_e_f_i_x_X_X_X_X_X_X_s_u_f_f_i_x, and the string XXXXXX is modified as
       for mmkksstteemmpp().

       The mmkkoosstteemmppss() function is to  mmkksstteemmppss()  as  mmkkoosstteemmpp()  is  to  mmkk‐‐
       sstteemmpp().

